  "notes": [
    "Meshes are shipped upstream as binary STL in metres, so unlike the 280 model no DAE conversion was needed.",
    "The upstream URDF declares effort=\"0\" velocity=\"0\" on every joint limit; PyBullet accepts this and the project's own FK/IK ignores effort/velocity.",
    "The upstream model has no separate flange link. joint6's rotation axis is (0,-1,0) of J5_Link and the J6_Link plate normal is -Y, so the tool axis is J6 -Y; the added flange frame encodes exactly that.",
    "No camera bracket ships upstream. The bracket and housing in configs/default.json are placeholder boxes, not real hardware."
  ]
